[MUST] DOTNET-NAMESPACE-DOTTED-PASCAL (namespace): Namespaces are dot-separated PascalCase segments that generally widen from an organization identifier down to more specific areas, something like Organization, then a product or technology area, then an optional feature and sub-area, rather than mirroring an internal team or org-chart structure; a namespace should never reuse the exact name of a type defined within it, or vice versa.
